                      (ntation_runtime.s):00013         ; FEAT-002 low-RAM presentation flow, copied to $1900 during GMC boot.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00014         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror begins. Canonical definitions:
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00015         ; wiki/internal/implementation/routine-catalog.html
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00016         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Inputs: Source and destination identities, bounded count or stream metadata, and any required mapped page
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00017         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Outputs: Copied, decoded, merged, cached, or addressed data plus caller-visible pointer progress
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00018         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00019         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Reads: The declared source stream, table, framebuffer rows, or metadata record
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00020         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Writes: Only the declared bounded destination record, cache, row range, or scratch fields
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00021         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Side effects: May temporarily map a required GIME page while moving or decoding data
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00022         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Invariants: Counts and destination bounds are honored; any temporary GIME mapping is restored before returning unless the routine contract explicitly states otherwise
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00023         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile input Inputs: PIA input state, prior sampled state, and axis or key selection
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00024         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile input Outputs: Normalized input state, edge bits, or axis sample
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00025         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile input Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00026         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile input Reads: PIA registers and prior input samples
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00027         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile input Writes: Owned input state and temporary PIA scan selection
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00028         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile input Side effects: Temporarily drives keyboard or joystick scan hardware
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00029         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile input Invariants: PIA control and drive state are restored to the runtime convention before return
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00030         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Inputs: Presentation state, interval timer, input edges, current map, and the selected auxiliary profile
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00031         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Outputs: Updated presentation state and the dispatcher retain/release status when applicable
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00032         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00033         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Reads: Presentation direct-page state, cold payloads, authored map streams, and input state
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00034         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Writes: Presentation state, mapped BACK pixels, and presentation-owned persistent metadata
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00035         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Side effects: May retain the foreground interval or produce a complete presentation surface
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00036         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Invariants: Gameplay simulation begins only after release; hidden hydration may prepare initial-stage state and hold it unchanged until release; FRONT publication remains IRQ-owned
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00037         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Inputs: Current render intent, selected actor or tile state, and a valid BACK or staging destination
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00038         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Outputs: Updated destination pixels and any owner-local history required by later restoration
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00039         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00040         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Reads: Authoritative gameplay state, immutable art streams, and current owner-local background metadata
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00041         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Writes: BACK or staging pixels, render scratch, and owner-local save-under or damage metadata
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00042         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Side effects: Changes a non-visible composition surface or its metadata
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00043         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile render Invariants: The routine never selects the visible FRONT surface; temporary PAR5 mappings expire or restore before return
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00044         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract cold_ptr profile=copy: Resolve a pointer into the currently mapped presentation cold payload.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00045         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract cold_read_byte profile=copy: Read one byte from the presentation cold payload while preserving mapping ownership.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00046         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract colour_surface profile=render: Apply a generated sparse nibble-colour stream to a selected 16-by-16 presentation surface.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00047         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract colour_tile profile=render: Replace every nonzero packed pixel pair in one selected 8-by-8 instruction tile.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00048         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract draw_actor_overlay profile=render: Draw the selected presentation actor stream into the current presentation destination.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00049         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract draw_cell profile=render: Draw cell.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00050         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract draw_tile_id profile=render: Draw tile id.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00051         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract PRES_MAIN_DYNAMIC_TEXT profile=render: Render one dynamic glyph or graphic descriptor at the supplied destination, routing glyphs to the shared mask-font renderer and graphics to the presentation blitter.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00052         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract draw_score_value profile=presentation: Render packed-BCD scores right-aligned within the caller-provided digit span, blanking leading zeroes, preserving internal zeroes, and showing an all-zero value as one zero.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00053         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract draw_score_value_digit profile=presentation: Render one score digit or a blank leading cell, set the significance flag when the first nonzero digit is encountered, and advance Y by one tile.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00054         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract gameplay_reentry profile=presentation: Restore gameplay mappings and state after presentation releases the interval.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00055         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract init_gameplay profile=presentation: Prepare the first level before its preview and skip the already initialized next-stage context.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00056         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract install_aux_runtime profile=presentation: Install aux runtime.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00057         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract map_back profile=copy: Map back.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00058         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract presentation_flow_tick profile=presentation: Dispatch the current presentation interval and return retain or release status.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00059         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract scan_keys profile=input: Scan keys and, in complete profile, route an eligible automatic-loop wake.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00060         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract start_screen profile=presentation: Initialize and draw the requested presentation screen.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00061         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract timer profile=presentation: Advance and return the current presentation interval timer.
                      (ntation_runtime.s):00062         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror ends.
